From: Hugo Malinen <patch@tokoro.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: x1e80100: emulate dual-edge wake IRQs

When the PDC runs in pass-through mode (Linux owns EL2, where the
qcom_scm_io_writel() to PDC_GPIO_INT_CTL_ENABLE succeeds), qcom-pdc turns
IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH on a GPIO wake IRQ into IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING. Without
the dual-edge errata emulation in pinctrl-msm, only one edge is ever seen.

On the Lenovo IdeaPad Slim 5x the lid switch (gpio-keys, GPIO 92, active
low) then fires only on lid open: closing the lid is never reported and
logind never suspends on lid close.

Enable wakeirq_dual_edge_errata so pinctrl-msm re-arms the PDC for the
opposite edge after each interrupt, as on sc7180 and others.

---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c
@@ -1837,6 +1837,7 @@ static const struct msm_pinctrl_soc_data x1e80100_pinctrl = {
 	.ngpios = 239,
 	.wakeirq_map = x1e80100_pdc_map,
 	.nwakeirq_map = ARRAY_SIZE(x1e80100_pdc_map),
+	.wakeirq_dual_edge_errata = true,
 	.egpio_func = 9,
 };
 
